1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:03,117
One photographer squeezed Paris's mail
onto a pigeon's tail.

2
00:00:03,517 --> 00:00:04,800
He had to escape first.

3
00:00:06,483 --> 00:00:08,967
Prussian armies ringed Paris and cut the
telegraph.

4
00:00:09,417 --> 00:00:11,100
Two million people were cut off.

5
00:00:12,517 --> 00:00:14,683
Balloons took mail out but couldn't
return.

6
00:00:15,067 --> 00:00:16,317
How would replies come?

7
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:19,667
Pigeons fly home from anywhere.

8
00:00:20,117 --> 00:00:21,550
Balloons carried them away.

9
00:00:22,417 --> 00:00:23,633
Birds can't carry much.

10
00:00:24,183 --> 00:00:27,483
Dagron had an idea: shrink pages to finger
size.

11
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:31,017
It had to happen in Tours, with the
government.

12
00:00:31,183 --> 00:00:32,350
So, a balloon.

13
00:00:33,417 --> 00:00:35,500
That morning another balloon was shot
down.

14
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:37,983
Dagron's dumped sand and climbed.

15
00:00:39,017 --> 00:00:41,783
He landed in Prussian territory and
escaped to Tours.

16
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,483
He filmed the letters, tied them to
pigeons' tails.

17
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:47,350
The film was projected.

18
00:00:47,717 --> 00:00:50,333
The tiny page grew, and Paris read its
mail.

19
00:00:52,783 --> 00:00:54,217
Most birds never returned.

20
00:00:54,683 --> 00:00:56,533
Those that did carried a city's letters.

